# CableDesk udev rules.
#
# Empty for this milestone. Per docs/UPSTREAM_INTEGRATION.md, the managed
# Sunshine runtime already ships its own udev rule granting the "uaccess"
# tag on /dev/uinput to the active graphical session's user, which is the
# upstream-recommended mechanism (not broad group membership — see
# engineering rule "no world-writable /dev/uinput"). CableDesk should reuse
# that rule rather than duplicate it; whether CableDesk still needs a rule
# of its own (e.g. for Thunderbolt/USB4-specific device nodes) is open —
# see docs/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md. Nothing here mutates permissions yet.
